Aerie-Purpose: Create and own the Filter Engine service from the browser's main parts, so it has a defined lifetime and no process-wide singleton.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc (ChromeBrowserMainParts creation), chrome/browser/BUILD.gn (source_set core deps)
Aerie-Kind: hook

One AddParts() call, in the same way as ChromeBrowserMainExtraPartsMemory. The
part (chrome/browser/aerie_adblock, in the overlay) creates the service in
PreProfileInit(), before any URLLoaderFactory for web content exists, and
destroys it in PostMainMessageLoopRun().

--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
@@ -36,2 +36,3 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/browser_process_impl.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/aerie_adblock/aerie_adblock_main_extra_parts.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main_extra_parts.h"
@@ -845,2 +846,5 @@
 
+  // Aerie: owns the Filter Engine service.
+  main_parts->AddParts(std::make_unique<AerieAdblockMainExtraParts>());
+
   chrome::AddMetricsExtraParts(main_parts.get());
--- a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
@@ -1108,2 +1108,3 @@
     "//chrome/browser/ai",
+    "//chrome/browser/aerie_adblock",
     "//chrome/browser/app_mode",
